ISAL1 package (version 1.00)   ---   README    ---
=========================================================================

This package contains Matlab implementations of an Infeasible-Point Sub-
gradient Algorithm (ISA) for the following L1-norm minimization problems:

* Basis Pursuit (this folder; main function: ISAL1.m)                
  	min ||x||_1  s.t.  Ax=b

* Basis Pursuit Denoising (ISAL1bpdn folder; main function: ISAL1bpdn.m)
  	min ||x||_1  s.t. ||Ax-b||_2 <= delta

ISA is an extension of the classical projected subgradient method that
replaces the usual exact projections onto the feasible set by adaptive
approximate projections. For Basis Pursuit, these are realized via a 
truncated CG procedure; for BP Denoising, they are obtained using FISTA.
(FISTA is described in Beck/Teboulle, "A fast iterative shrinkage-
thresholding algorithm for linear inverse problems", 2009; the code we 
use is a modified version of the proj_b2.m function from the UNLocBoX 
package by Puy/Perraudin, available at http://unlocbox.sourceforge.net/)

Note that the implementation of ISAL1bpdn is presently still a prototype;
algorithmic parameters are tuned for solving Basis Pursuit. We hope to 
improve on this aspect in a future release. 

Detailed descriptions of ISA can be found in the references listed in the 
files ISAL1.m and ISAL1bpdn.m. (See also the HOC Suite, available from 
http://wwwopt.mathematik.tu-darmstadt.de/spear/).

The codes may be used and modified as desired, but please retain the 
authorship/copyright information if you redistribute (possibly modified)
versions of any files from this package, and cite the above-mentioned 
respective reference(s) in your own work using ISAL1.

